.TH QUOKKA 1 "2026-11-01" "quokka 2.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quokka \- keep a small build cache warm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quokka
.RB [ \-\-warm\-up
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-evict\-after
.IR DURATION ]
.I COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quokka
keeps the entries of a build cache ready between runs. It is a made-up program, used to check that a
model reads a manual page before it answers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-warm\-up " N"
Load the
.I N
most recently used entries before the command starts. The default is 3.
.TP
.BI \-\-evict\-after " DURATION"
Drop an entry that has been idle this long, for example 90s or 10m. The default is 90s.
.TP
.B \-\-frozen
Never write to the cache. The command fails if an entry is missing.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the version and the state of the cache.
.TP
.B list
Print every entry with its size.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for a usage error, 70 when
.B \-\-frozen
finds a missing entry.
